Function strings allow you to do neat things.
BLD>Like bold your text...
CLRB>Or clear the terminal.
CONT>NOBR>Function strings use one to five characters followed by a less than sign (<).
They will be found and removed from anywhere in the line.
CLRB>Currently implemented- CLRA, CLRB, BLD, RED, YLW, GRN, BLU, PNK, PUR, LBLU, LME, ITAL, CONT, NOBR, ESC, SPD, PORT
CLRA clears the terminal after the line is displayed.
CLRB clears the terminal before the line is displayed.
BLD renders the text as bold.
RED, GRN, YLW, PNK, PUR, LBLU, LME, and BLU change the text color
CONT makes the text continue without waiting for input.
NOBR removes the full line between text.
SPD, ITAL and PORT use the greater/less than signs as parentheses to extract a value.
SPD allows you to set the speed of the text.
PORT will render a portrait before the text, like an RPG.
PORT<:3>Like this!
ITAL allows you to italicize text.
Like ITAL<this!>
ESC makes the line ignore all of these neat functions.
